# i18n

## Stack

- Library: `next-intl` with App Router locale routing
- Locales: `en` (default), `de`, `fr`, `it`
- `localePrefix: 'as-needed'` (English has no URL prefix)
- UI catalogs: `apps/web/messages/{locale}.json`
- Legal bodies: `apps/web/content/legal/{locale}/` (not in message JSON)
- Navigation: `@/i18n/navigation` (`Link`, `redirect`, `useRouter`, `usePathname`)
- Server redirects: `redirect({ href, locale })` and `return redirect(...)` for narrowing

## Copy rules (all locales)

- No em dashes (`—`). Prefer period, comma, colon, or parentheses.
- Keep a clean, modern, concise product tone across languages.
- Never claim Helvety can decrypt or recover encrypted content.

## German (`de`) only: Swiss High German

- Use Swiss orthography for the double-s sound: always `ss`, never `ß`.
- Examples: `Strasse`, `gross`, `heiss`, `dass`, `muss`, `Schliessen`.
- Write standard Swiss High German, not dialect.

## Before finishing i18n text changes

Search `apps/web/messages/` and `apps/web/content/legal/` for `—` and (in German) `ß`.
Keep policy version IDs in `CURRENT_POLICY_VERSIONS` unchanged for translation-only edits.
